    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149-a1-a7">

                <pb facs="0279" n="237" xml:id="pg237"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 6, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    note of the 4th instant, in reference to a paragraph which appeared in the Daily
                    News of the 17th ultimo, respecting the immediate preparation of the Sumter for
                    departure from the port of Liverpool. I must confess that the information
                    received by me from Liverpool from wholly independent sources had led me to
                    believe the newspaper statement to be true. It is, however, with very great
                    satisfaction I receive the contradiction of it from your lordship, as well as
                    the assurance that the movements of that vessel are under the observation of her
                    Majesty’s government. I am the more led to indulge this that the notice appears
                    to have been spontaneously furnished to me, with a degree of courtesy which I
                    should be wanting in my duty if I were to fail properly to appreciate.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
